    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nWhen using for instance\r\n\r\n```\r\nsr'`\r\n```\r\n( to replace ' with ` )\r\n\r\nafter the replacement the cursor is going to the far left of the surround. Could we get an option to change this behavior, so we have 3 options:\r\n\r\n- put the cursor on the left of the surround\r\n- put the cursor on the right of the surround\r\n- put the cursor back where it was before the replacement operation\r\n\r\n\r\n",
